## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component following official Vercel documentation
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency (v1.5.1)
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

### Implementation Details

1. **Package Installation**: Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm, adding 377 packages to the project.

2. **Analytics Integration**: Following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
   - Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout
   - This placement ensures analytics tracking is available across all pages

3. **Code Preservation**: All existing code structure was preserved:
   - Font configurations remain unchanged
   - Metadata configuration intact
   - Existing className and suppressHydrationWarning attributes maintained

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✅ ESLint passed with no issues
- ✅ All static pages generated correctly

### Next Steps

To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab in your Vercel project dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics

The Analytics component will automatically start collecting anonymous usage data once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
